      "body": "## Motivation\n\nAt small batch, decode issues one tensor-parallel all-reduce per attention block and one per MLP/MoE block: 129 per step for Qwen3-32B and 94 for Qwen3-30B-A3B at TP4. Their latency is a fixed part of every step. On Arc Pro B70 (4 cards over PCIe), oneCCL's default SYCL all-reduce takes 17-26 us per call at decode sizes. Its Arc-specific algorithm (`CCL_SYCL_ALLREDUCE_ARC=1`) takes 15-16 us, and it is equally fast at prefill sizes.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `distributed/bootstrap.py`: new `_set_xpu_ccl_defaults()`, called in `init_parallel_runtime` on XPU before the first communicator is created.\n  - When the device name contains `Arc`, it does `os.environ.setdefault(\"CCL_SYCL_ALLREDUCE_ARC\", \"1\")`, so a value the user sets still wins.\n  - Other Intel GPUs are left alone.\n- Setting the variable in-process takes effect: oneCCL reads it when the first communicator is created, and the per-call latency drops as shown below.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nOnly the all-reduce algorithm changes. Like any switch of all-reduce algorithm, the summation order can change, so outputs are not bit-identical across the two settings. oneCCL runs are not bit-reproducible on this setup to begin with.\n\nNo accuracy change is expected; the combined check below runs GSM8K with this PR applied.\n\n**Combined check on main** (`7e142dd9fd` with #46997-#47003 applied, sgl-kernel-xpu 0.5.0, 4x B70, TP4, the server flags listed under Speed Tests, GSM8K full 1319 sampled at 0.7 / 0.8):\n\n| model | GSM8K | c=1 median TPOT | c=4 median TPOT |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Qwen3-30B-A3B bf16 | 94.69% (95.38% in an earlier run without these PRs) | 6.74 ms | 10.68 ms |\n| Qwen3-32B-FP8 + EAGLE3 (`AngelSlim/Qwen3-32B_eagle3`, sampled verify) | 95.30% | 11.08 ms (accept length 2.37) | 13.97 ms |\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\n**Setup:**\n- 4x Arc Pro B70, TP4 on cards with no shared PCIe switch, torch 2.14.0+xpu.\n- compute-runtime 26.31, oneAPI 2026.0.\n\nAll-reduce latency per call, measured inside an XPU graph (bf16, 4 ranks):\n\n| message | default | `CCL_SYCL_ALLREDUCE_ARC=1` |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2048 x 1 | 18.5 us | 14.7 us |\n| 2048 x 4 | 26.4 | 14.7 |\n| 2048 x 16 | 24.9 | 15.2 |\n| 5120 x 1 | 16.6 | 14.6 |\n| 5120 x 32 | 22.9 | 20.6 |\n| 5120 x 4096 (prefill) | 2041 | 2041 |\n\noneCCL's low-latency variant (`CCL_SYCL_ALLREDUCE_LL=1`) is as fast in graphs, but it is 2x slower in eager mode (63-75 us vs 33-42 us), so it was not used.\n\nEnd to end, `bench_serving` random 512 in / 256 out, TPOT in ms, ABBA order:\n- A: this branch with `CCL_SYCL_ALLREDUCE_ARC=0`.\n- B: this branch's default.\n- Server flags: the cookbook BMG command (`--device xpu --tp 4`) plus `--attention-backend intel_xpu --page-size 64 --cuda-graph-backend-decode full --cuda-graph-backend-prefill breakable`.\n\n| model | c=1 A / B | c=4 A / B | c=16 A / B |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Qwen3-30B-A3B | 6.85, 6.84 / 6.73, 6.72 (-1.8%) | 11.00, 10.98 / 10.73, 10.72 (-2.4%) | 20.38, 20.45 / 20.15, 20.15 (-1.3%) |\n| Qwen3-32B | 31.58, 31.59 / 31.18, 31.18 (-1.3%) | 32.52, 32.56 / 32.17, 32.17 (-1.1%) | 34.93, 34.93 / 34.64, 34.52 (-1.0%) |\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). (No test: a test would only restate the `setdefault`.)\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41861260827](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41861260827)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41861260510](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41861260510)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41861260499](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41861260499)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
